BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Burning Monk: A Celebration of Thich Quang Duc
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260613T103000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260613T123000
UID:16664a93ae4c7c268d71d01c@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:Guest speaker Devamitra explores the life and significance of 
 Thich Quang Duc\, the Buddhist monk who immolated himself in Saigon on 11 
 June 1963. His act became one of the defining images of the twentieth cent
 ury\, drawing global attention to the persecution of Buddhists in South Vi
 etnam. He reflects on its meaning today and the heroic ideal in Buddhism.
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/burning-monk-13-jun
END:VEVENT
